# Rust
/target/
ockr-plugin-example/target/
ockr-plugin-typst-example/target/
# Cargo.lock is committed — ockr ships as a binary, so a locked,
# reproducible dependency set matters for anyone building from source.
# Same reasoning for the plugin crates: each builds to a final wasm
# artifact, not a published library, so their Cargo.lock is committed too.

